rator is zero, so the expression is zero. The inequality \\(\\frac{x + 6}{x^2 + 2x + 7} \\ge 0\\) is satisfied at \\(x = -6\\).\n\nThus, the solution to the inequality is the interval \\([-6, \\infty)\\). The final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{[-6, \\infty)}\n\\]",
